# RouteNote — Cursor Rules

RouteNote is an **offline-first** Flutter app (saved places, optional Google
Drive backup, opt-in Gemini "Smart Insights"). Full, pass/fail evaluation
standards for every area of the codebase live in
[AGENT_SKILLS.md](AGENT_SKILLS.md) — **read it before editing and before
finishing any task**, then run the verification gate (`flutter analyze lib test`
→ no issues, `flutter test` → all green).

## Non-negotiables (summary)

1. **Zero backend / offline-first.** No RouteNote server. App works fully
   offline. Network allowed only for: Drive sync while signed in, opt-in
   Gemini (`--dart-define=GEMINI_API_KEY`, key in `x-goog-api-key` header, never
   URL), map deep links, and short-link resolution. No new network dependency
   or endpoint host without justification.
2. **Persistence = Hive CE only** (`placesBox` + `settingsBox` via
   repositories). No direct `box.put` from widgets/providers.
3. **Riverpod 3.4.x.** `ref.watch` only in `build`; timers disposed via
   `ref.onDispose`; no needless rebuilds.
4. **i18n (EN/AR).** Every user-facing string in `app_en.arb` +
   `app_ar.arb`, used via generated `AppLocalizations`. Never hardcode.
5. **Silent Google Auth** via `attemptLightweightAuthentication()` —
   `GoogleSignIn.signInSilently()` was **removed in google_sign_in v7**; do not
   reintroduce. Drive restore only when the local list is empty.
6. **Sign-out keeps ALL local data** (zero data loss, per README). Sign-out
   clears the Google session + auth snapshot only — never `placesBox`.
   A data wipe is a separate, explicitly-confirmed feature.
7. **Secrets.** Never log raw transport errors or the Gemini key; gate
   `debugPrint` with `kDebugMode`. No tokens/keys/coordinates in release output.
8. **Locked/hidden places** are guarded by `BiometricService` (the only
   `local_auth` touchpoint); content reveals only after successful auth.
9. **Location parsing** through `LocationParser` only — maps-URL regex set +
   custom coordinate validation; every pattern has a unit test.
10. **Dark mode & RTL.** Colors from `AppTheme`/`colorScheme` (no hardcoded
    `Colors.white/black` except QR canvas); layout uses directional padding and
    must render correctly in Arabic.

> When in doubt, AGENT_SKILLS.md wins. Report per-area pass/fail with evidence
> per the "Reporting" section there.